.SH AUTH ON ACTION HOOKS
An auth on action policy can ask for a login again before these actions.
See
.B Auth On Action Policy
in
.BR otpme\-policy (1).
A device has the hooks every object type has, and these; a command of another name is in brackets:
.RS
.PP
.na
.nh
change_mac\ (mac).
.hy
.ad
.RE
.\" END AUTH ON ACTION HOOKS
.SH FILES
.na
.nh
.TP
\fI/var/lib/otpme/tree/\fR
The objects of the realm, on the nodes; devices are not synced to hosts.
A device is the directory \fI<device>.device\fR in the directory of its unit, e.g. \fI<realm>.realm/<site>.site/devices.unit/ip\-phone\-1.device/\fR, with its settings in \fIobject.json\fR.
Change them with the commands above, not in the file.
.hy
.ad
